# Hektor (Cursor)

Hektor is a QA authoring + triage methodology. The durable specs live once as
`.claude/skills/hektor-*/SKILL.md` (plain markdown — read them directly; they
are harness-neutral). This rule routes you to the right one and states the
non-negotiables so generated code passes the automated PR reviewer.

## Read before writing code

- **`.claude/skills/hektor-conventions/SKILL.md`** — the kernel for the
  **web-test** repo (`web-ui-test/`). Read BEFORE any `*Page.java`,
  `*Layout.java`, or `*Test.java`. It encodes every PR-reviewer rule
  (BLOCKER/WARNING) with the correct pattern.
- **`.claude/skills/hektor-resource-client/SKILL.md`** — the kernel for the
  **test-data-client** repo. Read BEFORE any `*ResourceClient.java` /
  `AbName.java` (`extends AbstractService`, `@Component`, `clients.*` URL shape,
  `@Slf4j`, SCREAMING_SNAKE enum).
- **`.claude/skills/hektor-orchestrator/SKILL.md`** — the router for the full
  methodology (journey-mapping → composing → coverage → triage → verify). Start
  here when the ask is "test this feature end to end".

Other skills by task: `hektor-test-composer` (one journey's whole portfolio),
`hektor-page-authoring` (page/layout objects), `hektor-journey-mapping`,
`hektor-coverage-expansion`, `hektor-flaky-triage`, `hektor-failure-diagnosis`,
`hektor-test-repair`, `hektor-edr-contract`, `hektor-visual-regression`,
`hektor-security-zap`, `hektor-from-jira`, `hektor-verify`,
`hektor-test-catalogue`, `hektor-work-summary-deck`, `hektor-bug-discovery`,
`hektor-qagent`.

## The PR reviewer gate (why this matters)

Every PR is scanned by a bot that marks it **Needs Work** on a BLOCKER. The
`.claude/hooks/pr-rules-gate.sh` gate mirrors those deterministic checks. On
Cursor it runs on **`afterFileEdit`** through `adapter.sh` and surfaces findings
as advisory feedback — Cursor has no reliable pre-edit block, so it can't *stop*
the write the way Claude Code does. Treat any Hektor finding it reports as a
must-fix before you open the PR. Never `new XxxPage()` / `new XxxLayout()`, no
XPath inside `@FindBy(css=…)`, no `getRemoteWebDriver()`/`getShadowRoot()` in a
test/layout, `@ScheduledDisable` needs a `reason`, `*ResourceClient` extends
`AbstractService` + `@Component`, `clients.*` URLs start with `/` and never
contain `//`. The full list + fixes are in the two kernel skills above.

## Enforcement in Cursor

Registered in `.cursor/hooks.json` via `adapter.sh` (the ECC-style shim that
runs the unmodified `.claude/hooks/*.sh` gates):
- **`beforeShellExecution`** → `commit-gate` (the agent doesn't `git commit` /
  `git push`; you commit and review the working tree yourself) — a real block.
- **`afterFileEdit`** → `pr-rules-gate` — advisory PR-rule findings.

Bypass a gate for a deliberate exception: its own env switch, e.g.
`HEKTOR_PR_RULES_GATE=off` / `HEKTOR_COMMIT_GATE=off`, or disable all Cursor
adaptation with `HEKTOR_CURSOR_HOOKS=off`.

This rule file is local to the repo and won't appear in any PR.
